INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (360,'AK0',132,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-14 15:38:52',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-14 00:00:00','2023-09-22 23:59:59','Material Planner','MP 001','165','0','','Lae',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Co ordination & Planning','Paradise Foods Limited, West Taraka site, currently has a vacant position in it’s Procurement &Supply Chain Department for enthusiastic and highly motivated individuals based in Lae. We have a vacancy for:\r\n\r\nMATERIAL PLANNER\r\n\r\nThis position reports to the Supply Chain Planner. The purpose of this position is to organise and plan raw material orders according to demand and quality standards and, to ensure goods are ordered on time for production runs in profitable manner. The goal is to ensure the smooth and cost-efficient flow if the production operations.\r\n\r\nThe Role:\r\n\r\nPlan and coordinate in liaison with Procurement Team on material ordering workflows for Taraka site.\r\nPlan and priorities ordering in liaison with Production planners to ensure maximum performance and minimum delay.\r\nEnsures raw materials are ordered and available to meet Demand Forecasts in a timely manner.\r\nAddress shipping issuesmaterial risks when they arise aiming for minimum disruption.\r\nPrepare and submit status and performance reports.\r\nKeep paperwork organized.\r\nCollaborate with quality control, warehouse, and other staff.\r\nLiaise with other Raw Material and FG Planners to ensure appropriate levels of inventory is achieved and always maintained.\r\nContribute to effective maintenance of companies MRP system with order suggestions and inventory levels.\r\nDevelopment and reporting of Raw Material inventory reports to S&OP.','About You:<br /><br />Degree in Business Management– preferably a Business degree in Communication/IT would be an advantage.<br />At least 2-3 years’ experience in a similar role or 5 years + experience in a similar role with proven track record in the role.<br /><br />Personal Attributes:<br /><br />Excellent written and verbal communication skills<br />Ambitious with a strong desire to learn and progress.<br />Energetic and proactive approach<br />Able to juggle priorities and manage time to meet deadlines.<br />Good team player<br /><br />Desirable:<br /><br />Experience in FMCG environment.<br /><br />If you think you are the right candidates for this role, do forward your written documents including your CV no later than 22nd September 2023 to:<br /><br />The Human Resources Coordinator<br />Paradise Foods Limited<br />PO Box 1441, Taraka Site, <br />Lae 411, Morobe Province<br /><br />Email: recruitment@paradisefoods.com.pg','1','Yes','12','36','8','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (361,'AK1',132,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-14 15:50:54',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-14 00:00:00','2023-09-22 23:59:59','Sales Merchandisers x 10','SM 010','165','0','','Mt. Hagen, Kundiawa, Goroka, Alotau, Vanimo, Popondetta, Port Mo',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Sales & Marketing','Paradise Company Limited is looking to recruit suitable, enthusiastic and motivated Sales Merchandisers to be based in the following locations reporting directly to the Trade Marketing Representatives responsible in each area;\r\n\r\nMt. Hagen x3\r\nKundiawa x1\r\nGoroka x1\r\nAlotau x1\r\nVanimo x1\r\nPopondetta x1\r\nPort Moresby x2\r\n\r\nMain Responsibilities\r\n\r\nThe Sales Merchandiser helps the workgroup achieve its purpose by performing sales activities in merchandising, promotions, sales displays, packing, sampling, cleaning, refilling and setting up shelves, and placing posters to meet the objectives of the daily sales operation plan.','About You:<br /><br />Minimum Grade 12 education.<br />Tertiary qualifications preferred.<br />Proficient with MS Office particularly MS Excel<br />Current Driver’s License (Class 3 or class 6);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (362,'AK2',132,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-15 02:13:47',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-14 00:00:00','2023-09-22 23:59:59','Trade Marketing Representatives x2','TMR 002','165','0','','Mt Hagen',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Sales & Marketing','Paradise Company Limited is looking to recruit suitable, enthusiastic, and motivated x2 Trade Marketing Representatives based in Mt. Hagen and reporting directly to the Area Field Manager.\r\n\r\nSkills and Knowledge\r\n\r\nUnderstands the market, key players and factors.\r\nFamiliar with consumer and trade trends\r\nUnderstands the basic Supply Chain\r\nUnderstand retail classifications.\r\nUnderstands outlet call and coverage planning.\r\nStrong Organizational Skills\r\nGood negotiation Skills\r\nAbility to learn and adapt and improvise quickly.','About You:<br /><br />Minimum of 3-5 years progressive experience in a sales related role<br />Tertiary qualifications preferred.<br />Proficient with MS Office particularly MS Excel<br />Have a current Driver’s License (Class 3 or 6);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (363,'AK3',44,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-19 08:01:13',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-18 00:00:00','2023-09-27 23:59:59','Production Shift Manager','PSM 001','165','0','','Lae',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Food Technology','Trukai Industries Limited is seeking a passionate and self-driven Production Shift Manager to join the Manufacturing Team. This role is based in Lae and will report to the Manufacturing Manager.\r\n\r\nAs the Production Shift Manager you will be fully responsible for planned production, inventory and stock control of raw & packaging materials. This also includes leading a team whose primary responsibility is ensuring production targets.\r\n\r\nYou will also be responsible for identifying and driving opportunities for continuous improvement across the manufacturing team as well as ensuring that the existing process & equipment are managed for optimum efficiency, cost & output and that plans and strategies are in place to develop the process to meet short, medium & long-term goals','Key Requirements<br />Bachelor Degree in Applied Sciences preferably in Food Technology<br />Minimum of 5 years’ experience in an FMCG company<br />An understanding of HACCP and GMP principles<br />Ability to lead and monitor production efficiency, including raw and packaging materials<br />Strong people-oriented leader with the ability to be hands on and build engagement across the workforce.<br />Highly developed interpersonal and communication skills, both written and verbal<br />Excellent time management and attention to detail<br />Strong planning and organizational skills<br />Must have a continuous improvement mindset<br />Proficient in OHSE protocols<br />Computer literate in Outlook, Microsoft Excel and MS Word<br /> <br />Interested applicants should address their applications to:<br /> <br />HR Business Partner – Operations and Risk<br />Trukai Industries Limited<br />P O Box 2129,<br />Lae 411<br />Morobe Province<br /> <br />Or email to humanresources@trukai.com.pg<br /> <br />Closing date: 27th September 2023','1','Yes','36','72','9','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
