INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (371,'AL1',73,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-20 15:50:53',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-20 00:00:00','2023-10-02 23:59:59','Collections Officer','BSPFPNG00523','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Finance,Lending','The position is based in Port Moresby. The successful incumbent will be responsible to provide effective support to the sales team to ensure that all BSPF policies and procedures are adhered to and an excellent level of customer service both internal and external are achieved.\r\n\r\nTitle		Collections Officer\r\nReference No	BSPFPNG00523\r\nLocation	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nTo ensure that all policies and procedures are robust and that all internal and external relationships are well established for when a recovery, is to take place.\r\nTo ensure that they are well versed with all aspects of the deal approval and settlement process. The officer will need an intricate knowledge of all aspects of asset finance and the insurance protections that are in place.\r\nTo maintain an excellent working relationship internally and externally with all stakeholders ensuring all potential loss is minimized.\r\nTo have strong communication skills, tight monitoring protocols and be an excellent time manager, reporting all potential issues directly to management.\r\nTo follow the collection and disposal procedure exactly to avoid any risk of legal come back on BSPF.\r\nTo have a strong working relationship with the sales and support teams to ensure that every effort is made to ensure clients effect their payments in a timely manner.\r\nTo ensure that any remedial action that is put in place by the Head of Operations is adhered to.\r\nTo ensure management of accounts up to 90days in arrears.\r\nTo have a strong experience in dealing with reconciliations for both repossessions costs and entry preparations.\r\nTo be capable of dealing with adverse behaviours with an open mind.\r\nTo prepare daily, weekly and monthly reports.\r\nTo have the focus to drive consistent diary noting on finPOWER.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />University Degree preferably in Accounting or Business Studies.<br />Good financial and analytical skills.<br />Good sales and marketing skills.<br />Good Credit & Risk management knowledge.<br />Good sales and marketing skills.<br />Prior experience (3-5 yrs. +);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (372,'AL2',73,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-20 16:07:29',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-20 00:00:00','2023-10-02 23:59:59','Lending Officers - Mt Hagen x2,Lae x1,Kokopo x2','BSPGPNG00423','165','0','','Mt Hagen, Lae, Kokopo',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Finance,Lending','The successful incumbent will be responsible to actively engage with new and prospect business’s that operate in the PNG market, that have the potential to borrow between 0 – K3M for Asset Financing.\r\n\r\nTitle		Lending Officers\r\nReference No	BSPGPNG00423\r\nLocation	Mt Hagen x2,Lae x1,Kokopo x2\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nTo actively engage and network with the Dealer Network to ensure that all possible lead generation is secured.\r\nTo be actively involved in promoting BSPF at appropriate events, functions or opportunities that will lead to business generation for BSPF in conjunction with the Executive Management team.\r\nTo support and implement sales directives and strategies as directed by Head of Sales and country Manager BSPF.\r\nDevelop effective plans to grow the lending and deposit volumes in order to achieve the profitability targets in accordance with the budget for the area/region.\r\nIdentify prospective business client in the area and develop new business portfolio at the same time ensure effective control in protecting significant deposits within portfolio of accounts.\r\nProcess and/or recommend approval of Business lending applications which are of quality standard in line with the Lending policy.\r\nAssess all credit analysis and ensure it is of high standard and meets BSPF requirements in consultation with Credit Department for review and approval.\r\nAssess performance trends of key growth potential clients and build relationships.\r\nMaintain and review existing loan accounts to ensure clients repayments are on target and take necessary corrective actions to reduce potential arrears.\r\nImplement sales promotion campaigns for specific growth potential market segments to increase loan volumes at the same time implement effective sales cycle program to maintain relationship and assess future business opportunities.\r\nMonitor budget and identify levels of business gain and portfolio growth against budget forecasts and report on variances on a quarterly basis.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />University Degree preferably in Accounting or Business Studies.<br />Good financial and analytical skills.<br />Good Credit & Risk management knowledge.<br />Good sales and marketing skills.<br />Prior experience (2 yrs+);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (373,'AL3',73,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-20 16:21:34',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-20 00:00:00','2023-10-02 23:59:59','Lending Support Officers x2','BSPFPNG00323','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Finance,Lending','The position is based in Port Moresby. The successful incumbents will be responsible to provide effective support to the sales team to ensure that all BSPF policies and procedures are adhered to and an excellent level of customer service both internal and external are achieved.\r\n\r\nTitle			Lending Support Officers x2\r\nReference No		BSPFPNG00323\r\nLocation		Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType			Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nTo ensure that they are well versed with all aspects of the deal approval and settlement process. A sound knowledge of all aspects of asset finance and the insurance protections that are in place.\r\nTo maintain an excellent working relationship internally and externally with all stakeholders ensuring all potential loss is minimized.\r\nTo have strong communication skills, tight monitoring protocols and be an excellent time manager, reporting all potential issues directly to management.\r\nEnsure that all service delivery standards are maintained at all time.\r\nEnsure that all approval conditions are met before settlement on all transactions.\r\nEnsure all Letters of Officer are executed correctly and signed by the appropriate legal entity.\r\nEnsure security to be held is correct as per approval.\r\nEnsure loan documents are prepared in accordance with the application and loan approval.\r\nRequest for Title search & company searches as need be.\r\nCheck loan details in the Loan Security Documentation is correct as per approval.\r\nWhen all documents signed & sealed correctly ensure that the support team complete the settlements as required under the invoice.\r\nEnsure the customer files are in order and current.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />Preferred Accounting or Business Studies qualifications.<br />Good financial and analytical skills.<br />Good Credit & Risk management knowledge.<br />Good sales and marketing skills.<br />Prior experience (2 yrs.+);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (374,'AL4',48,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-20 19:34:08',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-20 00:00:00','2023-10-03 23:59:59','Tyre Crew – Leading Hand','TCLH','165','0','','Hidden Valley',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Auto Motive','We are seeking to recruit a Tyre Crew – Leading Hand for our Mobile Fleet Maintenance Department. Reporting to the Tyre Specialist, the successful applicant’s core objective is to lead the Tyres team on rotating shifts to complete planned and unplanned tyre maintenance tasks safely.\r\n\r\nKey roles and responsibilities include:\r\n\r\nEnsuring quality tyre maintenance, repairs and servicing tasks in an appropriate time frame\r\nMaking sure all Compliance with all Systems of Work requirements for the position as per document PP0281 \"MFM Work Management Process\". Ensure mandatory quality pre-release and daily maintenance checks (DMC);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (375,'AL5',76,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-20 19:51:12',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-20 00:00:00','2023-09-27 23:59:59','Admin Assistant','AA 001','165','0','','Lae',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Administration','Are you ready to take your administrative skills to the next level? Hardware Haus Limited in Lae is looking for a dynamic and organized Admin Assistant to join our thriving team!\r\n\r\nAs the Admin Assistant, you\'ll play a vital role in ensuring seamless operations and supporting our company\'s success to new heights.\r\n\r\nWHAT YOU WILL DO:\r\n\r\nProvide efficient administrative support to various departments.\r\nManage schedules, appointments, and travel arrangements.\r\nAssist with document preparation, data entry, and record keeping.\r\nRespond to inquiries and provide excellent customer service.\r\nCollaborate with team members to ensure smooth operations.\r\nMaintain office supplies and equipment.','WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR:<br /><br />Diploma in Business Administration, Management, or a related field.<br />Strong organizational and multitasking skills.<br />Excellent communication and interpersonal abilities.<br />Proficient in MS Office Suite.<br />Previous administrative experience preferred.<br /><br />If you have what it takes, please send a brief cover letter addressing your relevant experience with your updated CV. <br /><br />Only short-listed candidates will be contacted for an interview.<br /><br />All applicants should apply by email only with Position Vacant – Admin Assistant in the subject line to:<br /><br />The Recruitment Officer – People & Culture<br />CPL Group, <br />PO Box 1663, <br />Port Moresby, <br />National Capital District, <br /><br />E-mail: careers@cpl.com.pg<br /><br />Applications close 5:00pm on Wednesday, September 27, 2023','1','Yes','0','','7','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (376,'AL6',155,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-20 23:36:10','2023-09-20 23:41:44',NULL,'2023-09-20 00:00:00','2023-09-27 23:59:59','Channel Manager - Digital Experience','CM 001','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Sales & Digital Marketing','Air Niugini Limited is seeking to recruit suitably qualified and experienced candidate to fill the position of Channel Manager - Digital Experience within the E-Commerce Department.\r\n\r\nThe primary purpose of this position is to provide management support to the E-Commerce Manager by providing business and technical support required for the Online Sales channel and related services with the key objective of selling seats on ANG using the Web (IBE);
