INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (381,'AM1',73,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-24 15:43:20',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-22 00:00:00','2023-10-06 23:59:59','Tactical Manager','BSPPG04723','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Security Management','This position is based in Port Moresby and will report to the Head of Security Services. The successful incumbent will be responsible for ensuring all BSP Cash In Transit Operations and or movements are carried out in line with BSP Security Services Standard Operating Procedures and Recognized Industry Standards.\r\n\r\nTitle		Tactical Manager\r\nReference No	BSPPG04723\r\nLocation	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nA risk assessment particular to the cash in transit operations and /or movement is conducted prior to any cash movement.\r\nAn operational order is prepared and approved for all cash in transit operations.\r\nAll cash in transit movements are carried out in line with BSP standard operating procedures and approved industry standards.\r\nAll operational equipment used in any operation and/or movement is in working condition and complies with legislation.\r\nAll operational equipment is appropriately assigned and all allocations are accurately recorded.\r\nAll cash in transit staff are regularly trained and tested to ensure competency.\r\nThe continuous review and testing of procedures, weapon handling and formations is carried out so tactics remain contemporary in the changing BSP operational and threat environment.\r\nProfessional advice on tactical operations is provided as required.\r\nA learning environment is provided to subordinate staff and to mentor their development.\r\nUndertake duties as directed by Management of Security Services.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />Diploma in Police or Military related field.<br />Proficient in oral & written English.<br />Proficient in general Desktop Microsoft Applications.<br />Excellent Weapons Handling skills.<br />Excellent knowledge in the skills and methodology used in the movement of high risk items by vehicle, aircraft and / or foot.<br />Proficient knowledge of Policies & Procedures.<br />Proficient knowledge of Safety and Security standards.<br />Proficient skills in Tactical First Aid.<br />Sound knowledge in PNG Law and Constitutional rights.<br /><br />Think you have the appropriate skills and experience to perform this role? <br /><br />Send your application and detailed CV to:<br /><br />The Head of Talent Management, BSP People & Culture via email jobs@bsp.com.pg.<br /><br />Please contact us should you require additional information. <br /><br />Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interviews.<br /><br />Applications close on Friday, 06th October, 2023.','1','Yes','0','','14','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (382,'AM2',105,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-24 16:35:33','2023-09-24 16:45:47',NULL,'2023-09-24 00:00:00','2023-09-29 23:59:59','Case Work Manager - Lae','CWM 001','165','0','','Lae',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Social Welfare','Case Work Manager - FemiliPNG\r\n\r\nObjective: To provide effective and efficient case management to clients who are the organization’s target population.\r\nReport to: Operations Director\r\nSupervisees: Case Workers\r\nLocation: Lae, Morobe\r\n\r\nQualification:\r\n\r\nGraduate of Social Work or related field/Degrees\r\nRisk Assessment Skills\r\nKnowledge in community resources and trained in counselling with the high risk populations.\r\nExperience in working with high-risk population (Family and Sexual Violence Survivors);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (383,'AM3',105,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-24 16:56:53','2023-09-24 16:57:43',NULL,'2023-09-22 00:00:00','2023-09-29 23:59:59','Support Worker - POM','SW 001','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Social Welfare','Femili PNG is a local NGO with its headquarter in Lae that runs Case Management Centres, which work closely with other stakeholders to deliver services to survivors of family and sexual violence and child abuse. Our target population are women, men or children who are survivors of intimate partner violence, sexual violence, sorcery accusation related violence and/or child abuse. We seek an exceptional individual for an exceptional job.\r\n\r\nObjective: To ensure that office is clean for staff and clients, and clients are attended to by respective caseworker timely. The position will also assist on the security monitoring and safety of client/s accessing the office for case follow-up.\r\n\r\nReport to: Case Work Manager\r\nLocation: Port Moresby, National Capital District\r\n\r\nQualifications, desired experience and characteristics:\r\n\r\nConfidentiality\r\nPrevious experience in working with NGO or civic organization catering to family and sexual violence survivors\r\nConfident, reliable and works in professional manner\r\nSafety management skills\r\nAbility to respond and confront an insecure situation\r\nEmotional Control\r\nObjectivity and works with integrity\r\nRead, write, comprehend and communicate clearly in English.\r\nKnowledge and understanding the issues of Family and Sexual violence.','Duties and responsibilities:<br /><br />Attend to the client if the caseworker is not available while the client is receiving particular services or making her/his statement at the partner agency’s location.<br />Liaise with the partner agency regarding specific client’s update and report back to the case worker, as appropriate<br />Assist the client by providing specific rules before the referral i.e. safe house rules and regulations.<br />Accompany the client during referral to the partner stakeholder i.e. safe house referral, as instructed by the caseworker.<br />Deliver client statement to the partner agency that is engaged on the client’s case as requested by the caseworker.<br />Escort the caseworker while transporting high-risk case and while at the partner agency’s location.<br />Assist caseworker in purchasing client items that are identified as urgent need while caseworker is attending to the client.<br />Ordering client’s stock items when they are low in stock.<br />Do client stock inventory and follow-up,<br />Place an order request to the log assist for purchase.<br />Maintain office cleanliness<br />Support logistic officer in securing the office safety by assisting in assessing visitors during meeting or case discussion.<br />Liaise with Case Work Manager for any client related issue.<br />Report any untoward issues to the supervisor immediately<br />Other duties assigned by the supervisor.<br /><br />HOW TO APPLY?<br /><br />Your application should include your resume with contact details of three referees, cover letter explaining how you meet the position criteria, and a copy of your recent police clearance and vaccination card.<br /><br />Applications can be addressed to <br /><br />Femili PNG HR, <br />P.O Box 616 Lae, <br />Morobe Province, <br /><br />and emailed to recruitment@femilipng.org<br /><br />For more information, email us at info@femilipng.org<br /><br />Applications closes on Friday 29th September 2023.','1','Yes','0','','7','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
