INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (408,'AO8',73,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-29 04:38:42',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-28 00:00:00','2023-10-05 23:59:59','Inspection Officer','BSPPG04923','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Real Estate,Valuation','The position is based in Port Moresby, and reports to the Team Leader Funding &Settlement. The successful incumbent will undertake property inspections and provide detailed reports in a timely manner and will arrange/liaise with Bank Authorized Valuers to undertake property valuations and provide the Valuation report to the requestor in Retail.\r\n\r\nTitle		Inspection Officer\r\nReference No	BSPPG04923\r\nLocation	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nAll Actions pertaining to each matter delegated by Team Leader Funding & Settlement.\r\nComplete inspections and inspection reports in a timely manner.\r\nEnsure to arrange valuations in a timely manner and follow with the Bank Authorised Valuer on the issuance of the Valuation report.\r\nWhere required assist the Funding and Settlement Officers, in creating/funding of loans and attending to settlements.\r\nMaintain close follow up with Key Stakeholders to ensure all outstanding matters/dealings are resolved in a timely manner.\r\nAt all times adhere to the rules, regulations and policies and procedures of the Bank and the BU. The highest levels of honesty, integrity and professionalism are to be demonstrated when carrying out duties, with importance to be placed on maintaining high levels of customer service.\r\nEnsure filing is up-to-date and items are recorded correctly before being archived.\r\nOther duties as delegated by management.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />Minimum of Grade 12 certificate.<br />Class 3 Drivers License.<br />Basic Technical Skills in Numeracy and Finance.<br />Basic Technical Skills in Filing and Record Management.<br />Basic Technical Skills in Lending Process.<br />Basic Technical Skills in Policies & Procedures.<br />Basic Technical Skills in Risk Management and Credit Processes.<br />Good and clear communication skills.<br />Comprehensive knowledge on the banks loan products and features.<br />Comprehensive knowledge on the banks FCUBS core systems especially those in regards to Lending.<br />3 years banking experience with 1 year of personal/corporate lending experience.<br /><br />If you think you have the appropriate skills and experience to perform this role, send you application and detailed CV to:<br /><br />The Head of Talent Management, BSP People & Culture via email jobs@bsp.com.pg.<br /><br />Please contact us should you require additional information. Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interviews.<br /><br />Applications close on Thursday, 5th October, 2023.','1','Yes','36','72','7','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (409,'AO9',155,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-29 04:55:28',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-29 00:00:00','2023-10-13 23:59:59','Executive Manager Catering And Apartments','EMCA 001','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Catering,Aviation','We are seeking a talented and experienced individual to join our dynamic team as an Executive Manager, responsible for overseeing both our airline catering department and our 70-bedroom apartment complex.\r\n\r\nThis challenging yet rewarding role requires exceptional organizational skills, a keen eye for detail, and a passion for delivering outstanding customer service. If you are a highly motivated individual with a passion for excellence, this is an exceptional opportunity to join our team.\r\n\r\nExecutive Manager Catering And Apartments\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n \r\nManage and lead the airline catering department, ensuring smooth operations and adherence to high-quality standards.\r\nOversee the preparation, packaging, and delivery of meals to airlines, coordinating with suppliers, chefs, and transportation teams.\r\nImplement and maintain strict hygiene and safety protocols in compliance with industry regulations.\r\nDevelop and maintain strong relationships with airline clients, understanding their requirements and providing exceptional service.\r\nMonitor inventory levels, track cost efficiencies, and optimize resources to meet financial targets.\r\nLead a team of dedicated professionals, providing guidance, training, and support to foster a positive work environment.\r\nManage the day-to-day operations of the apartment complex, including tenant inquiries, maintenance requests, and maintaining equipment.\r\nEnsure the cleanliness, safety, and overall upkeep of the apartment complex, coordinating with maintenance and housekeeping staff.\r\nConduct regular inspections to identify areas for improvement and implement appropriate solutions.\r\nDevelop and implement marketing strategies to attract and retain tenants, ensuring high occupancy rates.\r\nHandle tenant complaints and resolve issues promptly and professionally.','To be considered for this role you must possess:<br /> <br />Degree or tertiary qualifications in Catering or Hospitality and Management<br />Previous experience in airline catering, hospitality, or property management is highly desirable.<br />Demonstrated knowledge and experience in food safety and quality assurance management.<br />Trained and experienced in HACCP standards.<br />Strong leadership abilities with a proven track record of successfully managing teams.<br />Exceptional organizational and multitasking skills, with the ability to prioritize effectively<br />Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to build relationships with clients, tenants, and team members.<br />Sound financial acumen with the ability to manage budgets and achieve financial targets.<br />Attention to detail and a commitment to delivering exceptional customer service.<br />Flexibility to work in a fast-paced environment and adapt to changing priorities.<br />Proficiency in computer systems and software relevant to the role.<br /><br />We offer a competitive salary, benefits package, and a supportive work environment that encourages growth and development.<br /><br />If you thrive in a fast-paced environment and are ready to take on a diverse range of responsibilities, we would love to hear from you.<br /><br />To apply, please email a detailed CV with full supporting documentation, and a reliable telephone number/email contact to recruitment@airniugini.com.pg by COB Friday 13th October 2023','1','Yes','0','','14','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (410,'AP0',148,NULL,'jobsite','2023-09-29 06:49:38',NULL,NULL,'2023-09-28 00:00:00','2023-10-13 23:59:59','Transport Coordinator - Farm','TC 001','165','0','','Lae',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Transportation','Zenag Chicken is a 100% PNG family-owned poultry company and for more than 75 years, the Zenag family have pioneered poultry innovation in Papua New Guinea. Years of hard work and experience has seen us grow into one of our country’s largest poultry producers. Our high-quality products are distributed to supermarkets, wholesalers, food service distributors and farmers across our country.\r\n\r\nAbout the Role\r\n\r\nReporting to the Transport Manager, the role is farm based and is responsible for ensuring of the timely delivery of farm products to Lae and farm materials from Lae to Zenag farm.\r\n\r\nDuties:\r\n\r\nResponsible for conducting daily toolbox meetings\r\nResponsible for administering employee’s timecards\r\nResponsible for the issue of daily fleet checklist\r\nResponsible for verifying the fleet checklist\r\nResponsible for monitoring each fleet’s fuel burn\r\nResponsible for planning the Daily Journey Management Plan\r\nResponsible liaising with workshop department for fleet break downs\r\nResponsible for collecting all GPS reports','About You<br /><br />Must have at least grade 10 certificate or have a Tertiary qualification in business administration<br />Must have hands on experience in Microsoft Office, Excel & Outlook<br />Must be flexible with working hours<br />Must be able to work with minimum supervision<br />Must have excellent communication skills<br /><br />If you think you are a perfect fit for this role, Email your CV and a one-page cover letter with three current references to recruitment@zenagchicken.com or you can hand deliver to our Head Office located in Marsina Street,Opposite Lae International Hospital. <br /><br />All applications must be attention to The HR Manager.<br /><br />Please do not include all your certificates with your application but list them in your CV.<br /><br />ONLY short-listed candidates will be contacted for an interview.<br /><br />If you do not receive any calls from our HR department within a week after the closing date, it means your application was not considered successful and we thank you for your interest in joining Zenag Chicken.<br /><br />Closing date for submissions is Friday 13th October 2023.','1','Yes','0','','15','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (411,'AP1',158,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-02 04:10:31','2023-10-02 04:29:39',NULL,'2023-10-01 00:00:00','2023-10-20 23:59:59','Deputy Secretary Corporate Affairs - DJAGEX. 03','DJAGEX. 03','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Legal Administration','The Department of Justice & Attorney General is a Central Agency responsible for the administration of Legal and Justice Service in Papua New Guinea. The Department now invites expression of interest from suitable qualified individuals for the position of;\r\n\r\nDEPUTY SECRETARY CORPORATE AFFAIRS\r\n\r\nPURPOSE OF THE JOB\r\n\r\nThe Deputy Secretary Corporate Affairs positions responsible to provide an effective and efficient co-ordination and delivery of all Corporate Services to the Department through policy, planning and evaluation, financial management, human resources management, assets management, information communication technology, Library & Records Management branches through integrated functions and systems.\r\n\r\nPRINCIPLE ACCOUNTABILITIES\r\n\r\nProvision of efficient Corporate and General Administration Services to the Department through the Corporate Services Branches.\r\nEnsure effective implementation of directives/decisions of the Secretary.\r\n\r\nMAJOR DUTIES\r\n\r\nEnsure that the Department has an annual work plan in accordance with its Corporate Plan, and develop or review the Department’s Corporate Plan as and when required.\r\nDevelop and submit the Department’s annual budget to the Secretary in accordance with the Public Finance (Management);
