INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (414,'AP4',158,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-02 14:39:20','2023-10-02 14:39:48',NULL,'2023-10-02 00:00:00','2023-10-20 23:59:59','Regional Public Curator, Momase - DJAGPC.03','DJAGPC.03','165','0','','Lae',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Legal Administration','The Department of Justice & Attorney General is a Central Agency responsible for the administration of Legal and Justice Service in Papua New Guinea. The Department now invites expression of interest from suitable qualified individuals for the position of;\r\n\r\nREGIONAL PUBLIC CURATOR MOMASE\r\n\r\nPURPOSE OF THE JOB\r\n\r\nThe role of the Regional Public Curator Momase is to lead and manage the administration of the Momase Regional Office of the Public Trustee of Papua New Guinea.\r\n\r\nPRINCIPLE ACCOUNTABILITIES\r\n\r\nEnsure that all deceased estates without wills are efficiently administered in accordance with the Public Curators Act and the Wills, Probate and Administration Act, and those beneficiaries receive their legally entitled benefits within the timeframe required by law.\r\nEnsure that the property of minors\' and persons certified to be insane is protected and properly managed. Ensure that proper records are maintained of all estates registered and realized.\r\nEnsure that there is effective and efficient control of all financial records, procedures, processes for the Momase region deceased estates.\r\n\r\nMAJOR DUTIES\r\n\r\nAdminister the provisions of the Wills Probate and Administration Act, Public Trustee Act and any other related acts.\r\nSupervise and train staff of the Momase Regional Office.\r\nSupervise the management of deceased estate properties in Momase region.\r\nCarry out inspection and audits of estate business administered advice on management problems and prepare recommendations for Public’ Trustee’s approval.\r\nPrepare Court documents and other papers such as Affidavits, Statutory Declaration, etc. as directed by the Public Trustee’s legal division.\r\nPerform other duties as consistent with the above and when directed by the Public Trustee.\r\nConduct staff performance appraisals for the subordinates in a timely manner.\r\nPerform other duties as consistent with the above as and when directed by the Public Curator.\r\n\r\nREPORTING AND WORK RELATIONSHIP - INTERNAL\r\n\r\nReport to Deputy Public Trustee.\r\nLiaise with Public Trustee’s Legal division.\r\nLiaise with Estate and Property Trust Officers at Head Office.\r\nLiaise with the Accounts division of Head Office.\r\n\r\nREPORTING AND WORK RELATIONSHIP - EXTERNAL\r\n\r\nLiaise with Counterpart officers in Regional Offices.\r\nLiaise with all District Administrators throughout the Southern Region.\r\nPrivate Lawyers, both public Sectors and NGOs.Liaise with Provincial Land Officers.\r\nLiaise with Office of the Registrar General.\r\nLiaise with the Office of the Valuer General.\r\nLiaise with Hospitals and Health Clinics within the Southern Region','KEY COMPETENCIES & PREREQUISITES<br /><br />Qualifications<br /><br />Must have a Degree in Property Management.<br /><br />Knowledge<br /><br />Public Service (Management);
