INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (433,'AR3',73,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-03 21:04:01',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-03 00:00:00','2023-10-20 23:59:59','Head of Financial Reporting','HFR','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Finance,','Position Details\r\n\r\nTitle:		Head of Financial Reporting\r\nReference No:	BSPPG05123\r\nLocation:	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType:		Full-Time\r\n\r\nAbout the Role:\r\n\r\nReporting to the BSP Group Chief Financial Officer, the position of Head of Financial Reporting will be responsible for the finance and accounting activities for the Bank’s opera????on in Papua New Guinea.\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nDevelop a strong management reporting focus on performance measurement, linking trends in operational performance to strategic goals and financial results.\r\nManage the continuous improvement of standardized monthly management reporting routines and reports in BSP PNG, providing leadership to finance and accounting staff that supports the management reporting functions in the bank, and act as the key financial advisor to the Bank’s business divisions in the BSP PNG operations.\r\nManage the timely preparation of information for the Board of Directors, Executive Committee, stock exchange compliance reporting, taxation, and bank regulatory reporting. associated with BSP operations in the PNG Market.\r\nEstablish and maintain internal controls, systems, policies and procedures;\r\nCoordinate work with external professionals in relation to financial, management and regulatory reporting matters.\r\nSupport the senior executive team with commercial decision-making with regards to PNG operations.\r\nStrategize & implement where appropriate process improvements within the Strategic Business Unit.\r\nStrategize & implement internal training & development initiatives for the staff.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />University Degree in Finance, Economics or Business.<br />Certificate of Practicing Accountant (PNG CPA);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (preferably banking experience);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (or studying);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (434,'AR4',44,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-04 01:53:29',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-03 00:00:00','2023-10-13 23:59:59','Human Resources Business Partner','HRBP 001','165','0','','Lae',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'HR Management','Trukai Industries Limited is seeking a passionate and driven Human Resources Business Partner to join its Human Resources Team. \r\n\r\nThis role is based in Lae, Morobe Province and will report to the General Manager – Human Resources.\r\n \r\nThe HR Business Partner will work collaboratively with Senior Management and their respective teams in proactively delivering a positive and engaging employee experience.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\nBachelor’s degree in Human Resources Management\r\n8 years’ of generalist HR experience\r\nHR Business Partner experience in an FMCG Company\r\nFamiliar with PNG Labor Law\r\nAbility to exercise sound judgment, tact and discretion when dealing with sensitive confidential information\r\nExposure of multiple human resource disciplines including employee relations and performance management\r\nExcellent communication skills both written and oral\r\nGood people skills','Interested applicants should address their applications to:<br /><br />HR Administrator<br />Trukai Industries Limited<br />P O Box 2129,<br />Lae 411<br />Morobe Province<br /><br />Or email to humanresources@trukai.com.pg<br /> <br />Closing date: 13th October 2023','1','Yes','72','120','10','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (435,'AR5',73,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-04 14:32:44',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-04 00:00:00','2023-10-20 23:59:59','OFSAA Specialist','BSPPG05023','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'ICT,Banking','Based in Port Moresby and reporting to the Financial Controller Reporting the OFSAA Specialist will be responsible for managing and maintenance of the Oracle Financial Services Analytical Applications (OFSAA);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (436,'AR6',160,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-04 16:16:52',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-04 00:00:00','2023-10-17 23:59:59','Science Research and Consultancy Division x6','SRCD 006','165','0','','Port Moresby, Goroka',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Anthropology,Conservation','The National Museum & Art Gallery is the leading scientific and cultural organization charged with the duty to secure Papua New Guinea’s cultural future through preserving our historical past, conserving our natural heritage and to promote our contemporary culture. Through our research and education, we want to be a cultural pillar of nation building by promoting and\r\nsharing the knowledge about Papua New Guinea’s modern history and our rich and diverse natural and cultural heritage.\r\n\r\nWorking for the National Museum & Art Gallery can be both a challenge and an inspiration. At this time when we are expecting a shift in our organizational culture, we are seeking individuals who are self-starting and those who can work with us as in the spirit of a team. We invite applications for the following vacancies:\r\n\r\nSCIENCE, RESEARCH AND CONSULTANCY DIVISION\r\n\r\n1. NMSE.001	Project Consultant	(Gr.15, K49,790);
