INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (450,'AT0',44,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-10 00:36:55',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-09 00:00:00','2023-10-20 23:59:59','Sales x8','SM 008','165','0','','Buka, Autonomous Region of Bougainville-Kavieng, New Ireland Pro',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Sales & Marketing','Trukai Industries Limited have the following vacancies in the New Guinea Islands and Southern Region: \r\n \r\nSenior Sales Representative – Buka, Autonomous Region of Bougainville\r\nSales Merchandiser – Buka, Autonomous Region of Bougainville\r\nSales Merchandiser – Kavieng, New Ireland Province\r\nSales Merchandiser – Keravat, East New Britain Province\r\nSales Representative – Tabubil, Western Province\r\nSenior Sales Representative - Port Moresby, National Capital District \r\nSales Merchandiser - Port Moresby, National Capital District \r\nSales Representative – Port Moresby, National Capital District \r\n \r\nThese positions on a daily basis will report directly to their respective Area Sales Manager.\r\n \r\nYou will be responsible for the efficient day-to-day management of all sales, customer service and product image including the administration in your designated location. You will be the point of contact and have a strong ability to show case and drive sales through wide range of customers every day.','Key Requirements<br /> <br />Completed Year 12<br />Diploma in Business and a related field (Desirable);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (451,'AT1',73,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-11 03:44:08',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-11 00:00:00','2023-10-17 23:59:59','Credit Analyst','No BSPPG05223','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Analysis','The position is based in Port Moresby and and reports to the Senior Relationship Manager. The successful candidate will be responsible to manage a portfolio of business clients within the Bank’s Corporate/ Commercial lending segment and develop the business for each relationship, maximizing portfolio and bank’s profitability.\r\n\r\nTitle:		Credit Analyst\r\nReference: 	No BSPPG05223\r\nLocation:	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType:		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nEnsure all simple Lending applications, Credit Application, annual review are effectively and efficiently completed for specific clients.\r\nEnsure financial statements are carefully analysed and information is processed into Credit Lens which will assist Credit Department in the decision making.\r\nLoad the Credit Applications, Moody’s Report, Risk Grade, Financial Statements via Bizedoc to Credit Department for approval making sure data integrity is maintained at all times.\r\nComplete all temporary overdraft requests for business clients in line with current lending policy.\r\nMaintain constant with contact with Professional Valuers for property valuations, Lands Department for title search and company search in accordance with business laws and bank policy.\r\nProcess all new and/or increased lending applications, register and prepare documentation in consultation with Lending Support within reasonable turnaround time.\r\nMaintain effective communication with business client with regards to loan processes, documentation, for approved loans and establish contact with client lawyers to process settlement in a timely manner.\r\nEnsure drawdown of loans new/increase and/or partial conditions are met by clients and correct fees, interest rates and repayment schedule are appropriately applied in line with lending policy.\r\nAssist Lending Assistants to upgrade skill level on the job as part of learning and development process within the business unit.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />Tertiary qualifications preferably in Accounting or Business Studies.<br />Proficient in Microsoft Applications.<br />Excellent communication skills both in written & oral.<br />Intermediate Technical Skills in Risk Management.<br />Demonstrated strong understanding of BSP lending Policies & Procedures.<br />Demonstrated highly developed level of financial analysis & credit assessment skills.<br />Exceptional organizational skills.<br />5 years’ experience in Lending environment or similar role.<br /><br />If you think you have the appropriate skills and experience to perform this role, please send your application and detailed CV to:<br /><br />The Head of Talent Management, BSP People & Culture via email: jobs@bsp.com.pg.<br /><br />Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interviews.<br /><br />Applications close Tuesday, 17 October, 2023.','1','Yes','36','72','6','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (452,'AT2',8,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-11 04:00:30',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-10 00:00:00','2023-10-18 23:59:59','Manager – Facilities & Property Management Department','BPNG 0011','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Property Management','The Bank of Papua New Guinea is a Contemporary Central Bank and Regulator employing best practice in the development and implementation of Monetary Policy, conduct of Financial Sector Supervision and in ensuring an efficient, safe and well-functioning Payments System.\r\n\r\nThe Bank of Papua New Guinea invites expression of interest from suitably qualified and experienced individuals to fill in the following position is based in Port Moresby:\r\n\r\nMANAGER – FACILITIES & PROPERTY MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT.\r\n\r\nReporting directly to the Assistant Governor – Corporate Affairs Group, the Officer is to effectively and efficiently assist in delivering some of the following functional responsibilities;\r\n\r\nMaintain and service the office buildings to provide a secure and effective working environment. \r\nEnsuring that basic facilities and plant/equipment are well maintained to meet ongoing and long-term needs of the Bank. \r\nEnsuring that facilities/properties meet government regulations and environmental, health and security standards. \r\nOverseeing building projects, renovations or refurbishments. \r\nAdvising the Bank on increasing energy efficiency and cost-effectiveness. \r\nResolves service problems and manages relationships with external suppliers. \r\nManage Leases Agreements and Contracts for services including security, cleaning, catering, property maintenance and projects.','Education/Qualification/Skills/Experience/Competencies:<br /><br />Bachelor’s Degree in Building & Architecture, Property Management & Engineering or a related field.<br />Have a minimum of five (5);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (453,'AT3',8,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-11 04:20:57',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-10 00:00:00','2023-10-18 23:59:59','Human Resource Officer – Client Support Unit','BPNG 0012','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'HR Coordination','The Bank of Papua New Guinea is a Contemporary Central Bank and Regulator employing best practice in the development and implementation of Monetary Policy, conduct of Financial Sector Supervision and in ensuring an efficient, safe and well-functioning Payments System.\r\n\r\nThe Bank of Papua New Guinea invites expression of interest from suitably qualified and experienced individuals to fill in the following position is based in Port Moresby:\r\n\r\nHUMAN RESOURCE OFFICER – CLIENT SUPPORT UNIT\r\n\r\nReporting directly to the Manager – Client Support Unit within the Human Resource Department, the Officer is to effectively and efficiently assist in delivering some of the following functional responsibilities;\r\n\r\nWorkforce Planning, Recruitment and Selection, Performance Management & Employee Benefits Administration.\r\nReward and Recognition, Separation and Termination, Employee Relations, Statutory Compliance.\r\nDelivers Key Results in accordance with an annual agreement and the Department’s plans.','Education/Qualification/Skills/Experience/Competencies:<br /><br />Have a Degree in Human Resources, Industrial Psychology or related field from a recognized tertiary institution. <br />Must have at least 3 years’ experience in similar role. <br />Proficient in oral and written communication skills. <br />Sound knowledge in PNG Labor Laws & Acts.<br /><br />Interested applicants can download the relevant position descriptions from our website www.bankpng.gov.pg or email jobs@bankpng.gov.pg<br /><br />Written applications must be addressed to:<br /><br />The Manager, Human Resource Department<br />Bank of Papua New Guinea<br />P.O Box 121,<br />PORT MORESBY,<br />National Capital District<br /><br />We encourage submission of electronic applications via email address: jobs@bankpng.gov.pg.<br /><br />Applications close on Wednesday, 18th October 2023.<br />Authorised by: Ms. Elizabeth Genia, AAICD<br />ACTING GOVERNOR','1','Yes','36','72','8','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (454,'AT4',8,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-11 04:31:11',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-10 00:00:00','2023-10-18 23:59:59','Human Resource Officer – Administrative Support Unit','BPNG 0013','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'HR Coordination','The Bank of Papua New Guinea is a Contemporary Central Bank and Regulator employing best practice in the development and implementation of Monetary Policy, conduct of Financial Sector Supervision and in ensuring an efficient, safe and well-functioning Payments System.\r\n\r\nThe Bank of Papua New Guinea invites expression of interest from suitably qualified and experienced individuals to fill in the following position is based in Port Moresby:\r\n\r\nHUMAN RESOURCE OFFICER – ADMINISTRATIVE SUPPORT UNIT\r\n\r\nReporting directly to the Manager – Administrative Support Unit within the Human Resource Department, the Officer is to effectively and efficiently assist in delivering some of the following functional responsibilities;\r\n\r\nWorkforce Planning, Recruitment and Selection, Performance Management & Employee Benefits Administration\r\nReward and Recognition, Separation and Termination, Employee Relations, Statutory Compliance \r\nDelivers Key Results in accordance with an annual agreement and the Department’s plans \r\nBenefits administration, Contract administration, Job evaluation, Position descriptions \r\nRecords management, Statutory compliance terms and conditions administration\r\nAdministration of the Alesco HR and Payroll System, Delivers Key Results in accordance with an annual agreement and the Department’s plans','Education/Qualification/Skills/Experience/Competencies:<br /><br />Have a Degree in Human Resources, Industrial Psychology or related field from a recognized tertiary institution <br />Must have at least 3 years’ experience in similar role <br />Proficient in oral and written communication skills <br />Sound & technical knowledge in HR/Payroll Systems<br /><br />Interested applicants can download the relevant position descriptions from our website www.bankpng.gov.pg or email jobs@bankpng.gov.pg<br /><br />Written applications must be addressed to:<br /><br />The Manager, Human Resource Department<br />Bank of Papua New Guinea<br />P.O Box 121,<br />PORT MORESBY,<br />National Capital District<br /><br />We encourage submission of electronic applications via email address: jobs@bankpng.gov.pg<br /><br />Applications close on Wednesday, 18th October 2023.<br />Authorised by: Ms. Elizabeth Genia, AAICD<br />ACTING GOVERNOR','1','Yes','36','72','8','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (455,'AT5',8,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-11 04:41:45',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-11 00:00:00','2023-10-18 23:59:59','Senior Internal Auditor','BPNG 0015','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Auditing','The Bank of Papua New Guinea is a Contemporary Central Bank and Regulator employing best practice in the development and implementation of Monetary Policy, conduct of Financial Sector Supervision and in ensuring an efficient, safe and well-functioning Payments System.\r\n\r\nThe Bank of Papua New Guinea invites expression of interest from suitably qualified and experienced individuals to fill in the following position is based in Port Moresby:\r\n\r\nSENIOR INTERNAL AUDITOR\r\n\r\nReporting directly to the Manager – Internal Audit Unit, the Officer is to effectively and efficiently assist in delivering some of the following functional responsibilities;\r\n\r\nAssist the Department Management to develop and implement a strategic approach to meet the Bank’s current and future needs effectively and efficiently, including appropriate devolution of responsibilities to\r\ndepartments and consideration of appropriate outsourcing. \r\nAssist in evaluation and advice to Department Management on proposed Bank initiatives from a specialist professional perspective in regards to compliance, governance and internal control. \r\nProvide advice and assistance to Audit Manager with the application of audit policies and practices including risk assessment, quality assurance, control, compliance, investigation, reporting. \r\nExamine, evaluate and report to Department Management on the effectiveness and efficiency of Bank operations, systems and procedures.','Education/Qualification/Skills/Experience/Competencies:<br /><br />Bachelors’ Degree in Accounting, Business or related fields as well as qualification, certification and experience in internal audit and risk management. <br />Appropriate technical and professional experience in risk based auditing. <br />Personal attributes to work collaboratively as part of the audit team. <br />Appropriate interpersonal, data analytical and investigative skills.<br /><br />Interested applicants can download the relevant position descriptions from our website www.bankpng.gov.pg or email jobs@bankpng.gov.pg<br /><br />Written applications must be addressed to:<br /><br />The Manager, Human Resource Department<br />Bank of Papua New Guinea<br />P.O Box 121,<br />PORT MORESBY,<br />National Capital District<br /><br />We encourage submission of electronic applications via email address: jobs@bankpng.gov.pg.<br /><br />Applications close on Wednesday, 18th October 2023.<br />Authorised by: Ms. Elizabeth Genia, AAICD<br />ACTING GOVERNOR','1','Yes','0','','7','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (456,'AT6',8,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-11 04:54:03',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-10 00:00:00','2023-10-18 23:59:59','IT Auditor','BPNG 0016','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'IT,Auditing','The Bank of Papua New Guinea is a Contemporary Central Bank and Regulator employing best practice in the development and implementation of Monetary Policy, conduct of Financial Sector Supervision and in ensuring an efficient, safe and well-functioning Payments System.\r\n\r\nThe Bank of Papua New Guinea invites expression of interest from suitably qualified and experienced individuals to fill in the following position is based in Port Moresby:\r\n\r\nIT AUDITOR\r\n\r\nReporting directly to the Senior – IT Auditor, Internal Audit, the Officer is to effectively and efficiently assist in delivering some of the following functional responsibilities;\r\n\r\nTo efficiently and effectively perform assigned audits and contribute to the above functional responsibilities and be accountable to the Senior IT Auditor for responsibilities. \r\nPerform various IT audits of the Bank’s application systems and IT infrastructures in accordance with approved annual plans - either individually or as part of a team;\r\nDeliver Key Results in accordance with an annual performance agreement; \r\nDemonstrate proficiency in applying information systems audit principles, skills and techniques in reviewing and testing the Bank’s application systems and IT infrastructures of varying complexity;','Education/Qualification/Skills/Experience/Competencies:<br /><br />Bachelors’ Degree in IT or related fields as well as qualification, certification and experience in internal audit and risk management.<br />Membership in a professional association e.g ISACA, IIA.<br />Appropriate technical and professional experience in risk based auditing.<br />Personal attributes to work collaboratively as part of the audit team.<br />Appropriate interpersonal, data analytical and investigative skills.<br /><br />Interested applicants can download the relevant position descriptions from our website www.bankpng.gov.pg or email jobs@bankpng.gov.pg<br /><br />Written applications must be addressed to:<br /><br />The Manager, Human Resource Department<br />Bank of Papua New Guinea<br />P.O Box 121,<br />PORT MORESBY,<br />National Capital District<br /><br />We encourage submission of electronic applications via email address: jobs@bankpng.gov.pg.<br /><br />Applications close on Wednesday, 18th October 2023.<br />Authorised by: Ms. Elizabeth Genia, AAICD<br />ACTING GOVERNOR','1','Yes','0','','8','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
