INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (477,'AV7',154,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-12 22:41:16',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-12 00:00:00','2023-11-03 23:59:59','Base Maintenance Manager','BMM 001','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Aviation,Maintenance,','PNG Air Engineering Division is seeking for suitably qualified and self – motivated candidate for the position of Base Maintenance Manager base in Port Moresby. The Base Maintenance Manager is responsible to the Manager Aircraft Maintenance for the day-to-day functions of the division and shall be responsible to the Manager Aircraft Maintenance for the following:\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nGiving leadership and direction to the application of safety and quality management principles and practices in the conduct of aircraft maintenance activity.\r\nDemonstrating personal commitment to quality standards, service culture and professionalism and clearly communicating standards and expectations.\r\nEnsuring any hazard is reported using the company Safety and Quality Report form, PNGA005. /AQD system.\r\nEnsuring the facilities are appropriate for the planned work.\r\nEnsuring the office accommodation is appropriate for the management of the planned work.\r\nEnsuring the working environment is appropriate for the tasks being undertaken.\r\nEnsuring there are adequate storage facilities for parts, tools, equipment and materials.\r\nEnsuring there are sufficient competent personnel rostered to plan, perform, supervise, inspect and certify for all maintenance as required by the CAMG.\r\nEnsuring there are tools, equipment and materials to perform the planned tasks.\r\nEnsuring that all maintenance is correctly certified for and that records of maintenance carried out are retained safely and securely for the statutory period.\r\nProviding support to the LAMEs and the supervisors as required and in accordance with this Part 145 Exposition.\r\nEnsuring that the organization’s procedures and standards are complied with when carrying out maintenance.\r\nLiaising with the CAMG for any discrepancy between workload and available manpower\r\nEnsuring parts holdings are maintained to provide adequate spares to support the fleets to be maintained Uncontrolled.\r\nProviding assistance to the GM MRO an MAM in recruiting suitable candidates for a location.\r\nEnsuring that all maintenance required to be carried out at line and base stations, plus any rectification carried out during maintenance, is only carried out in accordance with approved data.','Qualifications<br /><br />Tertiary Qualified in Engineering, Aviation or equivalent.<br />Must have at least 10 years’ experience in the aircraft maintenance industry.<br />Must hold an ICAO annex 1 type license or equivalent.<br />Must have demonstrated good communication skills (both written/oral);
