INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (488,'AW8',48,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-14 17:52:35',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-13 00:00:00','2023-10-28 23:59:59','Fire Instrument Technician','HV 009','165','0','','Hidden Valley',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Fire Alarm Technician','We are currently seeking to recruit a Fire Instrument Technician for our Fixed Plant Maintenance – Site Services Department. \r\n\r\nReporting to the Site Services Electrical Shift Supervisor, the primary objective of this role is conducting Fire Systems Inspections and repairs in accordance to set standards and industry’s best practices in a safe and efficient manner ensuring availability with no faults.\r\n\r\nKey roles and responsibilities include:\r\n\r\nInstalling and programing fire alarm systems and equipment.\r\nTroubleshoot, repairs and maintains electrical distribution systems relating to fire alarms.\r\nEnsures site fire alarm systems and emergency electrical systems are operational.\r\nEvaluate damage to equipment and assess the extent of repairs required.\r\nAssist in fire safety inspections.\r\nConducting Inspections, tests and repairs on devices such as smoke detectors, sprinklers and dry stand pipe system.\r\nLiaise with the Electrical Shift Supervisor and the Maintenance Planning team regarding work plans to allow adequate preparation time for task allocation.\r\nIdentifying bottlenecks and use problem solving tools to identify system improvement opportunities.\r\nEnsure parts, consumables and expertise are available as scheduled to enable team leaders to allocate and supervisor work flow.\r\nManage consumables and used information for instrumentation repairs to enable controlled ordering of materials and timely delivery.\r\nReporting all accidents and incidents to immediate supervisor.\r\nCascade plan and objectives through the team to ensure all activities are focused on agreed outcomes.','Qualifications, Skills and Experience required:<br /><br />Hold a valid PNG Instrumentation Trade Certificate or Electrical Trade Certification.<br />3 years or more experience in a similar role.<br />Broad experience in all facets of electrical control and distribution equipment maintenance and repair.<br />Broad experience in fire detection and prevention systems.<br />Basic working knowledge of computerised maintenance systems.<br />Good communication skills, both written & oral.<br />Sound Planning and organisational skills.<br />Strong technical skills, with being able to analyse and solve problems.<br />Be Safety focused.<br />Have current class 3 or 6 PNG driver’s licence.<br />Prepared to work to flexible company roster and varying work hours as required.<br />Be able to work in a team & multi-cultural environment.<br /><br />The above role is Hidden Valley mine site based<br /><br />If you are interested in this exciting and challenging opportunity and confident, you have the skills, knowledge and experience to fulfil this role, then please apply by email to HDVRecruitment@harmonyseasia.com<br /><br />Application closes Saturday 28th October 2023','1','Yes','36','72','15','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
