INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (507,'AY7',121,NULL,'jobsite','2023-10-23 15:39:40',NULL,NULL,'2023-10-23 00:00:00','2023-11-03 23:59:59','Senior Research Officer - Pathology','KIKRD. 21','165','0','','Alotau',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Research and development','Kokonas Indastri Koporesen is currently looking to hire qualified and experienced individuals for the following vacancies at the Milne Bay Research Station in Punipuni, Maramatana LLG, Alotau.\r\n\r\nWe welcome applications from interested candidates for the position of:\r\n\r\nSenior Research Officer - Pathology\r\n\r\nPURPOSE\r\nThe Senior Research Officer Pathology– is to manage and control all existing and emerging diseases of coconut and other plant diseases including other cash crops, spices, fruits, vegetables, field and forage crops throughout the plantations of MBRS Punipuni, Alotau, Milne Bay Province. The Incumbent is also responsible for designing and implementing all pathology research trials and activities on the Research Station.\r\n\r\nESSENTIAL DUTIES\r\nConducts research in establishing the nature, cause, and designing control measures of all coconut palm diseases and coconut products.\r\nInoculates healthy plants with culture of suspected causal agents taken from diseased plants and studies effects to determine agents responsible for disease.\r\nIsolates disease-causing agent, studies habits and life cycle, and devises control measures to destroy or control the causal agent.\r\nStudies rates of spread and intensity of disease under different soil conditions, climate, and geography, and predicts outbreaks of plant diseases.\r\nDetermines kinds of plants and insects that harbor or transmit disease.\r\nStudies losses from deterioration of perishable coconut products in transit or storage and develops practices to prevent or reduce losses.\r\nDetermines presence of disease causing agents in seed stocks to reduce losses from seed borne diseases.\r\nConduct periodical surveillance and monitoring of major coconut diseases including other crop species grown and cultivated on station and also in the farmers field\r\nOther duties as assigned by the respective supervisor or Manager in charge.\r\n\r\nSUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES\r\nManages three (3);
