INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (534,'BB4',148,NULL,'jobsite','2023-11-02 16:37:06',NULL,NULL,'2023-11-02 00:00:00','2023-11-11 23:59:59','Senior Heavy Diesel Equipment Mechanic','ZC 001','165','0','','Lae',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Mechanical Repair & Maintenance','Zenag Chicken has pioneered the poultry industry in Papua New Guinea for over 75 years. We provide employment to over a thousand employees, with our Head Office based in Lae and our farm a few hours’ drive out of the city, along the Bulolo District.\r\n\r\nSenior Heavy Diesel Equipment Mechanic\r\n\r\nWe are recruiting a Senior Heavy Diesel Equipment Mechanic for our Workshop based in Zenag Farm.\r\n\r\nThis position requires you to maintain the standard repair and maintenance of all fleet and heavy equipment.\r\n\r\nDuties\r\n\r\nThe repair and maintenance of all company units\r\nTrain junior mechanics on manufacture standards and workplace safety\r\nEnsuring all job are done on time, tested and recorded before unit is released\r\nEnsuring that PMS Service is done as per manufacturer standard\r\nChecking of all parts to be ordered to all units\r\nResponsible to re-check all mechanic job, and the workshop and storage free from hazardous','Skills and Experience Required:<br /><br />Must possess a Trade Certificate in Heavy Diesel Engine Mechanic<br />Well experienced on Isuzu, Kenworth & Hino Trucks, Cummins engine, Komatsu Equipment,<br />Can Overhaul engines (Cummins, Isuzu, Toyota);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (535,'BB5',73,NULL,'jobsite','2023-11-02 19:26:00',NULL,NULL,'2023-11-02 00:00:00','2023-11-07 23:59:59','Information Security Compliance & Reporting Associate Analyst','BSPPG060','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'ICT Security,Risk Management','This position is based in Port Moresby and reports to Manager Information Security Governance and Risk. The successful incumbent will provide support and assist the Team Leader Information Security Compliance by reporting and maintaining security compliance activities, and create regular reporting throughout BSP Financial Services Group depending on the frequency of reports required.\r\n\r\nTitle:		Information Security Compliance & Reporting Associate Analyst\r\nReference No	BSPPG060\r\nLocation	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nAssist to implement or review security compliance strategy and approach and ensure compliance with PCI DSS, ISO27001, GDPR, local Central Bank regulations and prudential standards, contractual requirements and globally-recognized standards and guidelines.\r\nAssist to develop and maintain materials and tools to effectively manage and communicate information security compliance across the group.\r\nAssist to collect, analyze, and prepare reports required for management, regulators, and other relevant stakeholders as directed by the management.\r\nAssist by carrying out all security incidents for violations, track and ensure that the recommendations are implemented and complete to prevent recurrence of similar incidents.\r\nAssist regularly, analyze and provide effective solutions to address all security compliance issues to the appropriate stakeholders across the group.\r\nAssist to conduct periodic User Access Reviews on systems to detect any discrepancies and report any control breakdowns in all systems across the group.\r\nStay abreast of cybersecurity changes and any developments and its’ impacts on compliance programs across the group.\r\nAssist IS Analyst carry out any tasks delegated by the management team.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />Diploma or Degree in Information Technology or Certificate in Risk/Audit or Cyber Security.<br />Basic skills in Information Technology.<br />Basic knowledge of documentation (Policies, Standard Process & Procedures);
