INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (538,'BB8',174,NULL,'jobsite','2023-11-03 16:19:06',NULL,NULL,'2023-11-03 00:00:00','2023-11-10 23:59:59','2x Budget Officer','IRC 002','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Accounting,Taxation','The Internal Revenue Commission Act 2014 establishes the IRC as a Statutory Authority and the “Commission” consisting of the Commissioner General and the Commissioners, as the governing body of the IRC. The Internal Revenue Commission is responsible for the collection of most of PNG’s Tax Revenue.\r\n\r\nThe Commission is seeking qualified and experienced Finance & Accounting professionals with enthusiasm and drive to make positive contributions to IRC’s revenue collection objectives. The Commission has vacancies within the Finance & Accounting Division based in Port Moresby - HQ.\r\n\r\n2x BUDGET OFFICER\r\n\r\nPURPOSE\r\nTo prepare, collate, implement and monitor budget in line with the annual budget appropriation and cash flow.\r\n\r\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\r\n\r\nCollate information and prepare the IRC annual budget for submission to Dept. of Treasury.\r\nPrepare timely Quarterly Budget Review Reports to Dept. of Treasury.\r\nPrepare Cash Flow for grants received based on IRC Divisional budgets.\r\nMonitor Divisional expenditure against budget and do daily movement of funds in the IFMS.\r\nPrepare Bank Reconciliations.','EDUCATION QUALIFICATION, KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ATTRIBUTES<br /><br />Minimum Bachelor Degree in Accounting, Business management or equivalent.<br />CPA membership is highly desired or working towards a CPA.<br />3 + years of experience in accounting and budgeting.<br />Knowledge of Taxation Laws, PNG Finance Management Act, National Procurement Act, Public Financial Management regulations or the ability to quickly acquire it.<br />Knowledge of Accounting standards, models, methodology.<br />Strong Budgeting and Accounting Competency Skills.<br />Strong Analytical, Reporting and Presentation Skills.<br /><br />For further information and/or job descriptions are required interested candidates may contact the Recruitment Team at recruitmentofficer@irc.gov.pg and/or Phone 307 7095/307 7102/3077117/3226958.<br /><br />Closing Date: Friday 10th November 2023<br /><br />Interested candidates should apply with a covering letter, along with an updated copy of resume (spelling out work experience and 3x referees);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (IRC);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (539,'BB9',73,NULL,'jobsite','2023-11-03 16:29:14','2023-11-03 16:29:37',NULL,'2023-11-03 00:00:00','2023-11-17 23:59:59','Executive Assistance','BSPPG061','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Finance,','We are seeking a highly skilled and experienced Financial Controller Reporting to join our team. As the Financial Controller Reporting, you will be responsible for managing and overseeing the internal stakeholder reporting function of the business. You will play a critical role in providing accurate and timely financial information to the Executive Management team to enable informed decision-making. The role reports to the Group Chief Financial Controller (GCFO);
