INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (545,'BC5',116,NULL,'jobsite','2023-11-06 01:24:48',NULL,NULL,'2023-11-03 00:00:00','2023-11-13 23:59:59','Property Officer','MRDC 001','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Real Estate,Property Mangement','MRDC requires the services of a creative, energetic, result-oriented and dedicated individual for the position of Property Officer.\r\n\r\nReporting to the Property Manager - PPT, the incumbent will act as the point of contact to current tenants, marketing and signing in of new tenants, manage and maintain the designated property’s operations including routine maintenance and service, attend to tenant complaints and issues, facilities management services include the upkeep of the building, monitoring house-keeping staff, tenant record keeping and outstanding payment and dealing with legal matters such as property damage claims and handling insurance related matters.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities:\r\n \r\nProperty management services.\r\nMarketing of vacant office spaces.\r\nManagement of Tenancy Lease Agreements in conjunction with Legal Division.\r\nArrange inspection, take-over, and hand-over work of building occupancy.\r\nEnsure periodic service to the standby gensets are undertaken as per schedule.\r\nArrange meetings with tenants where necessary.\r\nKeep track and issue notices for lease renewals and terminations on a timely basis.\r\nConduct period inspections.\r\nReport any damages and handle property cases relating to insurance claims.\r\nCarry out improvement and enhancement plans for the buildings.\r\nExecute the management of building security tasks.\r\nManage emergency situations.\r\nPromote tenant awareness of keeping the building environment safe.\r\nManage the building’s repair and maintenance work.\r\nCustomer services management (especially on complaint handling);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (546,'BC6',136,NULL,'jobsite','2023-11-06 04:11:12',NULL,NULL,'2023-11-06 00:00:00','2023-11-17 23:59:59','Corporate Communications Officer - Air Niugini Limited','VAN 001','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Public Relations,Communications','Air Niugini Limited is the national airline of Papua New Guinea, based in Port Moresby. It operates a domestic network as well as international services in Asia, Oceania, and Australia. Its main base is Jacksons International Airport, Port Moresby.\r\n\r\nApplications are invited from qualified and experienced professionals for this position based in Port Moresby.\r\n\r\n1x Corporate Communications Officer\r\n\r\nReporting to the Chief Corporate Communications Officer, this role is responsible for developing and executing public relations campaigns for Air Niugini. The roles are also responsible for managing the company\'s social media presence and developing and maintaining relationships with key media outlets.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities:\r\n\r\nDevelop and execute public relations campaigns for Air Niugini\r\nManage the company\'s social media presence\r\nDevelop and maintain relationships with key media outlets\r\nWrite and edit press releases, media advisories, and other public relations material\r\nRepresent Air Niugini at public events and trade shows; and\r\nManage the company\'s crisis communications plan.','Experience & Qualifications:<br /><br />Bachelor\'s Degree in Public Relations, Communications, or a related field<br />5+ years of experience in public relations or corporate communications<br />Experience in developing and executing public relations campaigns<br />Experience in managing social media platforms<br />Experience in developing and maintaining relationships with the media<br />Experience in the airline industry a benefit, though not essential<br />Strong understanding of the public relations and corporate communications industry<br />Excellent writing and editing skills<br />Ability to work independently and as part of a team.<br /><br />Air Niugini is an equal opportunity employer with excellent remuneration and benefits available, commensurate with qualifications and experience.<br /><br />To apply for this position:<br />Please visit our website: https://vanguard.com.pg/vacancies/<br />Complete the online application form and attach an updated CV, including details of three (3);
