INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (695,'BR5',48,NULL,'jobsite','2023-12-26 17:20:12',NULL,NULL,'2023-12-26 00:00:00','2024-01-05 23:59:59','Truck Driver','HV 012','165','0','','Hidden Valley',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Logistics,Trucking','We are seeking to recruit an experienced Truck Driver for our Commercial – HV Logistics Department.\r\n\r\nReporting to the Logistics Supervisor, the successful applicant will be responsible for safely operating Semi Trailer Trucks and providing escort support. This includes moving open deck loads, containers, dangerous goods within the Mine site roads and from time to time along Site Access Road between Bulolo and Hidden Valley Mine.\r\n\r\nKey roles and responsibilities include:\r\n\r\nAdhere to safe work practices including policies and procedures\r\nSafety-first mindset\r\nEscort trucks around site as required\r\nOperate sidelifter for moving ISOtainers\r\nOperate confidently & correctly on steep roads\r\nOperate within specified gears and speed limits\r\nFollow and correctly apply emergency brake procedures\r\nAdhere to Site traffic rules\r\nCorrectly restrain loads\r\nManage fatigue','Qualifications, Skills and Experience required:\r\n\r\nMinimum of 2 years Mine Site Semi Trailer Driving – highly desirable\r\nPrior mining experience – highly desirable\r\nExperience driving automatic 6x6 trucks\r\nSide lifter trailer operation - desirable\r\nCapable of speaking, reading and writing in English language\r\nMust have 5 years’ Experience Operating on Highways\r\nMust have class 4 & 6 current PNG Driver’s license\r\nMust have experience driving on steep roads\r\nStrong focus towards safety\r\nThe above role is Hidden Valley mine site based\r\n\r\nIf you are interested in this exciting and challenging opportunity and confident, you have the skills, knowledge and experience to fulfil this role, then please apply by email to;\r\n\r\nHDVRecruitment@harmonyseasia.com\r\n\r\nNote: Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted\r\n\r\nApplication closes on Friday, 05th January, 2024','1','Yes','12','36','10','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (696,'BR6',44,NULL,'jobsite','2024-01-01 15:46:27',NULL,NULL,'2024-01-01 00:00:00','2024-01-10 23:59:59','Stock Fumigator','TRU 010','165','0','','Lae, Morobe Province',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Food Technology','Trukai Industries Limited has a vacancy for afoo in our Inbound Logistics Department based in Lae, Morobe Province. This position will report to the Quality Control Shift Supervisor.\r\n\r\nThe Stock Fumigator is responsible for fumigating raw materials and finished products following the fumigation cycle. It also requires the incumbent to implement safe and quality practices daily in accordance with the site work plan activity.\r\n\r\nKey Requirements\r\n\r\nDiploma in Applied Science and Food Technology.\r\n2 years’ experience in similar role.\r\nMust be experienced or trained in Integrated Pest Management.\r\nMust be trained on relevant Quality Control SOP to carry out role effectively.\r\nGood analytical skills and a team player.\r\nAble to work with minimal supervision.\r\nGood personnel hygiene and habits.\r\nCommunicates well both orally and written.\r\nMust have good work ethics.\r\nDetail oriented.','Interested applicants should address their applications to:<br /><br />Human Resources Business Partner<br />Trukai Industries Limited<br />PO Box 2129<br />Lae 411<br />Morobe Province<br /><br />Closing date: 10th January, 2024<br /><br />To apply send your CV and other relevant documentation to humanresources@trukai.com.pg','1','Yes','12','36','9','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (697,'BR7',130,NULL,'jobsite','2024-01-01 16:28:10',NULL,NULL,'2024-01-01 00:00:00','2024-01-12 23:59:59','General Manager-Madang','DIG 012','165','0','','Madang',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Management,Operations','The General Manager is responsible for the overall management of a region to ensure delivery of revenue targets and revenue growth through effective management of the team and establishing presence and relationships with clients and customers. This role is based in Madang.\r\n\r\nMain Duties and Responsibilities:\r\n\r\nDelivering Sales Targets – Monthly \r\nMeet monthly handset and recharge targets as per targets sent out on a monthly basis from Head Office\r\nDelivering of Customer Service, Branding, Technical, TV, Finance, Fleet Management & HR KPI Targets\r\nResponsible for managing the region by managing new business opportunities and resource requirements and ensuring new initiatives are implemented within the specified timeframes.\r\n\r\nAccountable for the following regional responsibilities:\r\n \r\nResponsible for financial performance, Opex management, budget development, and day to day financial transactions\r\nEnsure all team members have an up to date DPR and monthly meetings are held with employees\r\nAll staff reviews are completed within the Mid-Year and Full Year timeframes and are calibrated prior to submission\r\nNetwork uptime is maintained in accordance with Digicel KPI – all network issues are reported in real time to the appropriate technical team members. A weekly report is provided to the Sales and Distribution Director on network performance and issues.\r\nAll new promotions are executed in alignment with timeframes. All Digicel branding is maintained in accordance with branding guidelines\r\nEnsure all vehicles are inspected weekly and prior to any usage, to ensure maintenance is minimal and there is limited downtime. A vehicle maintenance program is developed and implemented.\r\nAll disciplinary issue are managed in real time in partnership with the HR team\r\nResearching & reporting on competitor activity and identify sponsorship activities/opportunities for the Region.\r\nAll financial processes and procedures are completed in accordance with audit requirements and company policy. Any issues or discrepancies are reported immediately to Finance team.\r\n\r\nTeam Relationship\r\n\r\nInspire, lead and motivate a regional team including franchise, marketing, commercial, service delivery and capabilities to achieve the regional goals and objectives\r\n\r\nBusiness Compliance\r\n\r\nEnsure a sound understanding of, and demonstrate commitment to and comply with all legislation & telecommunications policies relevant to your role and all activities undertaken.','Academic qualifications and experience:<br /> <br />Degree qualification in business is preferred<br />5 year’s minimum managerial experience preferably within FMCG or Telco industry.<br />Must have leadership experience<br />Must hold Class 3 or 6 driver’s license with experience with manual gears<br /><br />Functional skills:<br /> <br />Excellent presentation skills required, both oral and written<br />Selling and negotiation skills<br />Results driven and proactive<br />A team player who is able to interact with persons at all levels<br />Excellent interpersonal skills<br />Good planning and organizational skills<br />Sociable – Excellent networking skills<br />Good working knowledge of the Microsoft Office Suite particularly Excel and PowerPoint<br /><br />Apply Today via <a href=\"mailto:PNG.Recruitment@digicelpacific.com\">PNG.Recruitment@digicelpacific.com </a><br /><br />Applications close 12 January 2024<br />','1','Yes','36','72','11','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
