INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (706,'BS6',73,NULL,'jobsite','2024-01-02 22:36:49',NULL,NULL,'2023-12-28 00:00:00','2024-01-10 23:59:59','Senior Data Analyst','BSPPG07523','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Analysis','Based in Port Moresby and reports to the Senior Manager Retail Operational Risk. The Senior Data Analyst – Retail Operational Risk role is responsible for leveraging advanced data mining, analytics and visualisation techniques to support and strengthen Retail Bank\'s operational risk managements daily operations and strategies. This role is crucial role in ensuring the effective identification, monitoring, and mitigation of operational risks across the Retail banking operations.\r\n\r\nTitle:		Senior Data Analyst\r\nReference No	BSPPG07523\r\nLocation	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nDevelop and implement advanced risk management strategies utilizing data mining, analytics, and visualization techniques.\r\nApply advanced data mining techniques within established security policies to extract profound insights and detect potential risk issues.\r\nDesign and create operational risk dashboards for daily operations and strategic decision making.\r\nCollaborate with the Senior Manager Operational Risk to establish real-time risk indicators and proactively identify areas under stress, potential hazards, and negative impacts.\r\nWork closely with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless integration of data insights into operational processes.\r\nProvide high-level regular and ad-hoc reports to the Senior Manager Retail Operational Risk.\r\nDrive continuous improvement initiatives, staying abreast of industry trends, evolving data analytics techniques, and best practices.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />Bachelor\'s degree or Masters in Data Science or relevant field.<br />7-10 years of experience in data analytics, preferably in the banking or financial sector.<br />Experience in developing and maintaining real-time dashboards;<br />Demonstrate experience in data visualisations;<br />Proven experience in data analysis, risk management, and visualization.<br />Proficient in data mining tools and techniques.<br />Strong communication and collaboration skills.<br />Proficient in data mining, predictive analytics, and statistical modelling.<br /><br />Think you have the appropriate skills and experience to perform this role? Send your application and detailed CV to:<br /><br />The Head of Talent Management, BSP People & Culture via email jobs@bsp.com.pg.<br /><br />Please contact us should you require additional information. Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interviews.<br /><br />Applications close on Wednesday, 10 January, 2024.','1','Yes','72','120','13','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (707,'BS7',73,NULL,'jobsite','2024-01-02 22:42:01',NULL,NULL,'2023-12-28 00:00:00','2024-01-10 23:59:59','Senior Retail Operational Risk Analyst','BSPPG07423','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Retail,Risk Analysis','Based in Port Moresby and reports to the Senior Manager Retail Operational Risk. This role is pivotal in safeguarding the BSP Retail SBU Operations by collaborating with Retail management to proactively identify, analyze and financial loss and negative impacts ensuring the resilience and success of Retail SBU.\r\n\r\nTitle		Senior Retail Operational Risk Analyst\r\nReference No	BSPPG07423\r\nLocation	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nUtilize data to obtain the necessary insights for informed decision-making.\r\nMonitor, assess, and report on the effectiveness of mitigation actions, strategies, and plans.\r\nMonitor insurance coverage for new ventures or business activities.\r\nBased on internal and external audit items work with management to resolve.\r\nOversee operational incident screening and escalation processes are adhered to.\r\nAnalyze and report daily on the extent of threats presented by operational incidents.\r\nCollaborate with the documentation team to complete risk and control assessments for key business processes.\r\nEnsure the development and maintenance of Risk & Control Assessments for key business processes.\r\nSupport the design and implementation of new controls or enhancements.\r\nRegularly evaluate the effectiveness of risk management policies, procedures, and mitigation activities.\r\nMaintain up-to-date knowledge of industry trends and best practices.\r\nProvide training and guidance to direct reports.\r\nCoordinate with Group ORM for ongoing awareness and training on operational risk policies.\r\nEnsure Retail staff are equipped to complete risk and control assessments.\r\nMaintain the Retail Compliance Obligations register.\r\nConduct regular tests on compliance-related internal controls.\r\nConduct regular Anti-Money Laundering control assessments.\r\nMonitor general compliance with internal policies, procedures, and external regulations.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />Minimum Bachelor’s degree in Business Management, Finance, Accounting or other related field.<br />Professional certification with an organization, such as the Governance Institute of Australia or the Operational Risk Management Institute.<br />Advanced knowledge of Risk Management and Operational Risk Management tools.<br />Familiarity with Risk monitoring systems<br />Minimum 5 years’ experience in a financial institution;<br />Specific exposure in an area related to data analysis, internal audit and compliance;<br />Past experience to support sound understanding of audit methods;<br />Past experiences to support sound understanding of compliance risk management.<br />Experiences to support sound understanding regulatory environment.<br /><br />Think you have the appropriate skills and experience to perform this role? Send your application and detailed CV to:<br /><br />The Head of Talent Management, BSP People & Culture via email jobs@bsp.com.pg.<br /><br />Please contact us should you require additional information. Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interviews.<br /><br />Applications close on Wednesday, 10 January, 2024.','1','Yes','36','72','13','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (708,'BS8',73,NULL,'jobsite','2024-01-02 22:52:50',NULL,NULL,'2023-12-28 00:00:00','2024-01-10 23:59:59','Retail Operational Risk Support Officer','BSPPG07323','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Retail,Risk Support','Based in Port Moresby and reports to the Retail Operational Risk Analyst. The successful incumbent will be responsible for providing support to the Senior Retail Operational Risk Analyst and Retail Operational Risk Analyst to identify threats proactively, analyze and measure the impact to the SBU.\r\n\r\nTitle		Retail Operational Risk Support Officer\r\nReference No	BSPPG07323\r\nLocation	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nProvide administrative assistance to the Senior Retail Operational Risk Analyst and Retail Operational Risk Analyst, ensuring documentation related to risk management activities are maintained and up to date.\r\nSupport in the maintenance and upkeep of the overall Retail SBU Risk Register, Business Unit and Branch risk registers.\r\nSupport in the maintenance and upkeep of the Business Unit and Branch key risk or control indicators;\r\nSupport document status of mitigation and/or remedial actions/strategies/plans.\r\nSupport documentation during risk and control assessments.\r\nSupport SBU risk reporting, standard and ad hoc.\r\nSupport maintenance and upkeep of risk training and awareness schedules, registers, assessments, evaluation sheets and content.\r\nReview operational incidents reported daily and ensure all necessary details are provided in the report and escalation processes adhered to.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />Bachelor’s degree (or higher);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (709,'BS9',73,NULL,'jobsite','2024-01-02 22:59:00',NULL,NULL,'2023-12-28 00:00:00','2024-01-10 23:59:59','Retail Operational Risk Analyst','BSPPG07223','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Retail,Risk Analysis','Based in Port Moresby and reports to the Senior Retail Operational Risk Analyst. The successful incumbent will support the senior analyst proactively identifying threats, analyze and measure the impacts to the SBU, work with Retail functions to determine and institute mitigation or resolution strategies and continuously assess and monitor these strategies to completion.\r\n\r\nTitle		Retail Operational Risk Analyst\r\nReference No	BSPPG07223\r\nLocation	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nAssist in the daily screening of operational incidents and ensure incident reports are detailed.\r\nContribute to the analysis and reporting on the extent of threats presented by operational incidents.\r\nAssist in the development and maintenance of Risk & Control Assessments for key business processes.\r\nSupport in monitoring, assessing, and reporting on the effectiveness of mitigation actions, strategies, and plans.\r\nContribute to tracking and resolving internal and external audit items within prescribed timeframes.\r\nSupport in the design and implementation of new controls or enhancements.\r\nParticipate in regular evaluations of the effectiveness of risk management policies, procedures, and mitigation activities.\r\nAssist Business Units and Branches with the upkeep of risk registers and key riskindicators.\r\nContribute to ongoing awareness and training on operational risk policies.\r\nContribute to maintaining the Retail Compliance Obligations register.\r\nParticipate in regular tests on compliance-related internal controls.\r\nCollaborate in monitoring compliance with internal policies, procedures, and external regulations.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />Bachelor’s degree (or higher);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (PNG);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (710,'BT0',73,NULL,'jobsite','2024-01-02 23:07:27',NULL,NULL,'2023-12-28 00:00:00','2024-01-10 23:59:59','Data Analyst','BSPPG07123','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Data Analysis','Based in Port Moresby and reports to the Senior Data Analyst – Operational Risk and is responsible for building reports to inform Retail SBU business decisions and leverage data to improve business processes.\r\n\r\nTitle:		Data Analyst\r\nReference No	BSPPG07123\r\nLocation	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey Deliverables:\r\n\r\nSupport the development of strategies to reduce risk exposures and enhance profits through data mining and analytics.\r\nMine and present financial and non-financial data, to detect actual or potential risk issues.\r\nDevelop visual aides and real-time dashboards for various stakeholders.\r\nSupport create risk indicators for identifying areas under stress, potential hazards, and negative customer impacts.\r\nFoster the development of Retail Operational Risk staff through training in data mining, analytics, and visualization.\r\nProviding guidance and support to Retail staff in areas of analytics and visualization.','Essential Qualifications, Professional/Skills and Experience:<br /><br />Bachelor\'s degree or Masters in Data Science or relevant field.<br />Minimum of 3-5 years of experience in data analytics, preferably in the banking or financial sector.<br />Experience in developing and maintaining real-time dashboards;<br />Demonstrate experience in data visualisations;<br />Proven experience in data analysis and risk management.<br />Proficient in data mining tools and techniques.<br />Strong communication and collaboration skills.<br />Proficient in data mining, predictive analytics, and statistical modelling.<br /><br />Think you have the appropriate skills and experience to perform this role? Send your application and detailed CV to:<br /><br />The Head of Talent Management, BSP People & Culture via email jobs@bsp.com.pg.<br /><br />Please contact us should you require additional information. Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interviews.<br /><br />Applications close on Wednesday, 10 January, 2024.','1','Yes','36','72','13','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
