INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (712,'BT2',117,NULL,'jobsite','2024-01-03 21:27:14',NULL,NULL,'2024-01-03 00:00:00','2024-01-20 23:59:59','Customer Services Officer Benefits','NS 002','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Customer Relations','Nambawan Super is currently seeking to recruit a suitably qualified, experienced and highly motivated individual for the position of Member Services Officer Benefits for their Member Benefits Division within the Customer Services Department, based in Port Moresby.\r\n\r\nThe successful candidate will report to Team Leader Member Benefits and be responsible for the reviewing and processing of all types of Benefits Payments and Housing Advance Payments within the expected Service Levels.\r\n\r\nSkills and experience required:\r\n\r\nMinimum of Diploma in Management, Finance and Business Administration is preferred.\r\nMinimum 2 years in similar role.\r\nMust possess sufficient knowledge of Superannuation Legislations and Regulations.\r\nMicrosoft Office Proficient.\r\nStrong Communicator, both written and verbal.\r\nGood planning and organisational skills.\r\nA self-starter and can work under minimum supervision.\r\nTeam player\r\nResult driven and pays attention to detail.','<div style=\"text-align: left;\">To apply for the position, please submit a cover letter outlining why you are suitable for the position, your resume with experience and qualifications. <br /><br />Please forward your application and credentials including 3 current referees to:<br /><br />Recruitment Team<br />Nambawan Super Limited<br />PO Box 483 Port Moresby NCD<br />Papua New Guinea<br /><br />Or alternatively email to: recruitment@nambawansuper.com.pg<br /><br />Application Close: Wednesday, 20 January 2024.</div>','1','Yes','12','36','17','Yes','Yes','','',0,0.000000,0.000000,'No');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (713,'BT3',73,NULL,'jobsite','2024-01-03 21:39:36',NULL,NULL,'2024-01-03 00:00:00','2024-01-17 23:59:59','Head of Data & Analytics','BSPPG07623','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Banking,Analytic','We are actively seeking a Head of Data & Analytics to drive strategic data initiatives, and champion a culture of data-driven decision-making within the organization. Reporting directly to the Group Chief Financial Controller, this pivotal role involves spearheading a central team of analytics professionals encompassing business analysts, data engineers, governance stewards, and business intelligence experts. Collaborating closely with key business stakeholders, you\'ll play a vital role in implementing our data analytics strategy and executing high-impact initiatives.\r\n\r\nTitle		Head of Data & Analytics\r\nReference No	BSPPG07623\r\nLocation	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey tasks & responsibilities\r\n\r\nDevelop and implement a comprehensive data and analytics strategy aligned with the organization\'s business objectives\r\nLead and manage a high-performing team of business analysts, data analysts, and BI developers\r\nLead the recruitment and selection process for key positions within the data and analytics team, ensuring alignment with organizational goals and requirements\r\nCollaborate with business units to identify opportunities for leveraging data to drive business outcomes\r\nOversee the collection, storage, management, quality and protection of data\r\nOversee the development and maintenance of data models, algorithms, and analytical tools\r\nDrive the design and implementation of data governance and data quality frameworks\r\nEnsure compliance with regulatory requirements related to data management and analytics\r\nDetermine where to priortise investment into analytics initiatives\r\nProvide strategic guidance on the adoption of emerging technologies in data and analytics\r\nFoster a data-driven culture within the organization through training and awareness programs\r\nCollaborate with IT teams to ensure seamless integration of data and analytics solutions\r\nEffectively communicate the status, value, and importance of data collection to executive members and staff\r\nEffectively manage consultants and vendors, ensuring seamless integration and alignment with internal team goals and methodologies\r\nKnowledge of relevant applications, big data solutions, and tools','Qualifications & experience<br /><br />Minimum of 15 years of experience in data and analytics roles, with at least 5 years in a leadership capacity<br />Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (e.g., Computer Science, Data Science, Business Analytics);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (Master’s or MBA);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (e.g., CDO, Data Science);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (714,'BT4',73,NULL,'jobsite','2024-01-03 21:51:32',NULL,NULL,'2024-01-03 00:00:00','2024-01-17 23:59:59','Data Governance Lead','BSPPG07723','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Data Analysis','We are actively seeking a Data Governance lead to spearhead pivotal data governance initiatives within our organization. Reporting directly to the Head of Data and Analytics, this role holds the responsibility of ensuring the integrity, security, and optimal usage of our data assets. Your leadership will be crucial in implementing and maintaining robust data governance frameworks, fostering a culture of compliance, quality, and strategic data management across the organization.\r\n\r\nTitle:		Data Governance Lead\r\nReference No:	BSPPG07723\r\nLocation:	Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea\r\nType:		Full-Time\r\n\r\nKey tasks & responsibilities\r\n\r\nDevelop a comprehensive data governance framework for the organization\r\nDevise and lead a program to implement the data governance framework\r\nLead and manage the Data Governance office, overseeing a team of 3 data stewards\r\nDefine and enforce data policies, standards, and procedures to ensure data quality and integrity\r\nCollaborate with stakeholders to identify critical data elements and establish data ownership\r\nConduct regular data quality assessments and implement corrective measures as needed\r\nEstablish and chair a Data Governance Council to oversee data governance initiatives\r\nWork closely with IT and business units to ensure alignment of data governance practices\r\nCreate and maintain a metadata management system to track data lineage and usage\r\nProvide guidance on data classification, data access controls, and data retention policies\r\nConduct training sessions to raise awareness and promote adherence to data governance standards','Qualifications & experience<br /><br />Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (e.g., Information Management, Data Science);
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (e.g., DGSP, CDMP);
