INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (863,'CI3',35,NULL,'jobsite','2024-07-22 00:13:52','2024-07-22 00:14:31',NULL,'2024-07-15 00:00:00','2024-08-09 23:59:59','CIVIL/STRUCTURAL ENGINEER','job#9907','165','0','','Port Moresby',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'• Bachelor’s Degree in Civil/Structural Engineering or equivalent. • Current Registered Member of IEPNG or equivalent. • Familiar with civil/structural engineering design applications such as Stead Pr','Reporting to the General Manager Projects Engineering, the Civil/Structural Engineering will lead all civil/structural design, engineering and construction for projects in buildings and infrastructure based onshore, nearshore and offshore, and remote operations.','<ul>\r\n<li>Lead all matters of civil/structural engineering from design changes and development, engineering reviews, construction reviews, acceptance of site changes, compliance with codes and standards.</li>\r\n<li>Manage the structural engineering change register.</li>\r\n<li>Oversee the development of structural engineering project briefs, technical specifications, and designs including drawings and bill-of-quantities.</li>\r\n<li>Lead the structural engineering procurement processes based on the bill of quantities.</li>\r\n<li>Continually review the project scope of structural works to schedule deliverables and forecast estimated costs based on the earned schedule progress.</li>\r\n<li>Oversee all onsite to monitor compliance with PNG building and safety regulations.</li>\r\n<li>Ensure all Subcontractors meet structural engineering contractual conditions of performance.</li>\r\n<li>Carryout technical and feasibility studies and draw up blueprints that satisfy technical specifications.</li>\r\n<li>Prepare internal and external reports pertaining to schedule progress.</li>\r\n<li>Conduct on site investigations and analyse data (maps, reports, tests, drawings and other);
