INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (964,'CS4',244,NULL,'jobsite','2024-10-02 05:54:59',NULL,NULL,'2024-09-30 00:00:00','2024-10-07 23:59:59','GENERAL MANAGER LAE OPERATIONS','job#0610','165','0','','Lae, Morobe Province',0,'0','No',NULL,NULL,'Bachelor\'s degree in civil engineering,business,management,related field or MBA;','Water PNG has an exciting job opportunity and is seeking an experienced General Manager Lae Operations reporting to the Chief Operating Officer at its office in Port Moresby.\r\nThe General Manager - Lae Operations oversees the branch, field operations, and activities of Water PNG. He/she develops business strategies and manages staff in line with the corporate and regulatory policies. Their responsibilities include creating new business opportunities, up scaling team productivity, and developing methods to improve branch profitability.','• Provide strategic direction and leadership to ensure effective operation and maintenance of water and sewerage treatments works and water distribution and sewerage networks in compliance with the NCD Water and Sewerage Act and the achievement of objectives defined in the Water PNG Strategic Plan;<br />• Track budgets and negotiate contracts;<br />• Oversee the preparation of budget estimates, negotiating and managing budget allocations according to the Water PNG Financial Manual;<br />• Plan, manage and coordinate the activities of the Lae Operations Department to ensure they achieve the objectives defined in the Water PNG Strategic Plans, Annual Business Operational Plans and Department Work Plans ensuring budget compliance;<br />• Provide essential input as a member of the Management Team to eky projects, strategic matters; and decision making process in the best interest of Fund or its stakeholders as applicable;<br />• Monitor and identify operations associated with new products and services, customer types, geographies, and channels;<br />• Ensure that the team operates to the highest standard of ethical conduct and complies with its “Workplace Charter and Code of Conduct”; and<br />• Oversee the development of strategies in reducing Non-Revenue Water (NRW);
